Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Datacenter Remains Uninitialized
Symptoms: Datacenter status shows Uninitialized even after creation.

Solution:

Verify that at least one storage domain is attached to the datacenter
Check storage domain status - it must be Active
Ensure NFS server is accessible and export paths are correct
Verify firewall settings on storage server
Commands to verify NFS connectivity:

# Test NFS mount from RHVM host
showmount -e storage-server.lab.local
mount -t nfs storage-server.lab.local:/storage/data /mnt/test
Issue 2: Storage Domain Activation Fails
Symptoms: Storage domain shows Inactive or Unknown status.

Solution:

Check NFS server status:
systemctl status nfs-server
systemctl status rpcbind
Verify export configuration:
cat /etc/exports
exportfs -v
Check network connectivity:
ping storage-server.lab.local
telnet storage-server.lab.local 2049
Issue 3: Network Configuration Problems
Symptoms: Networks show Non-operational status or VMs cannot communicate.

Solution:

Verify VLAN configuration if using tagged networks
Check physical network connectivity
Ensure proper network labels on hosts
Verify firewall rules allow required traffic
Best Practices for Datacenter Management
Performance Optimization
Storage Configuration:

Use dedicated storage networks when possible
Implement storage multipathing for redundancy
Monitor storage performance regularly
Network Design:

Separate management, storage, and VM traffic
Use appropriate VLAN segmentation
Implement network bonding for high availability
Resource Planning:

Plan for growth in storage and compute resources
Implement proper backup strategies
Monitor resource utilization trends
Security Considerations
Access Control:

Implement role-based access control (RBAC)
Use strong authentication mechanisms
Regular audit of user permissions
Network Security:

Implement network segmentation
Use firewalls to control traffic flow
Enable encryption for sensitive communications
